<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Francis - DSL for your Elixir web application</title>
  <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/nunito.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= tw_css %>">
  <link rel="icon" href="<%= favicon_ico %>">

  <meta name="description" content="A lightweight DSL for building Elixir web applications with HTTP actions, WebSockets, static content serving, and more.">
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://francis.build">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:title" content="Francis - DSL for your Elixir web application">
  <meta property="og:description" content="A lightweight DSL for building Elixir web applications with HTTP actions, WebSockets, static content serving, and more.">
  <meta property="og:image" content="https://francis.build<%= ogp_png %>">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="Francis">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  <meta property="twitter:domain" content="francis.build">
  <meta property="twitter:url" content="https://francis.build">
  <meta name="twitter:title" content="Francis - DSL for your Elixir web application">
  <meta name="twitter:description" content="A lightweight DSL for building Elixir web applications with HTTP actions, WebSockets, static content serving, and more.">
  <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://francis.build<%= ogp_png %>">

  <script src="<%= hljs_js %>" defer></script>
  <script src="<%= hljs_elixir_js %>" defer></script>
  <script src="<%= app_js %>" defer></script>
</head>
<body class="bg-white text-gray-900 antialiased selection:bg-hat selection:text-white">

  <a href="#get-started" class="sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:absolute focus:top-4 focus:left-4 focus:z-10 font-mono text-sm text-gray-900 bg-white ring-1 ring-gray-200 rounded-lg px-3 py-2">Skip to get started</a>

  <!-- Hero: warm light tint, hat stays visible -->
  <header class="bg-hat-subtle">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-20 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-28">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-8">
        <img src="<%= icon_webp %>" width="32" height="24" class="w-[2rem] h-auto" alt="">
        <p class="font-mono text-4xl font-bold text-hat">Francis</p>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-700 bg-white/70 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full ring-1 ring-gray-200">v<%= francis_version %></span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 leading-tight max-w-2xl text-balance">
        <span class="sr-only">Francis: </span>A small DSL for Elixir web apps. <span class="text-hat">Nothing more than you need.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="font-display text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mt-6">
        HTTP, WebSockets, SSE, and static files &mdash; without the ceremony. Two commands to start. Two to deploy. Built on
        <a href="https://github.com/mtrudel/bandit" class="text-link">Bandit</a>
        and
        <a href="https://github.com/elixir-plug/plug" class="text-link">Plug</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-3 mt-8 font-mono text-sm">
        <a href="https://hexdocs.pm/francis/readme.html" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 min-h-11 text-gray-900 hover:text-hat transition-colors">
          Read the docs
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" class="w-4 h-4" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.22 14.78a.75.75 0 0 0 1.06 0l7.22-7.22v5.69a.75.75 0 0 0 1.5 0v-7.5a.75.75 0 0 0-.75-.75h-7.5a.75.75 0 0 0 0 1.5h5.69l-7.22 7.22a.75.75 0 0 0 0 1.06Z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
          </svg>
        </a>
        <a href="https://github.com/francis-build/francis" class="inline-flex items-center min-h-11 text-gray-700 hover:text-gray-900 transition-colors">
          View on GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">

    <!-- Get started + Deploy: two-up on desktop, stacked mobile -->
    <section id="get-started" class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 pt-14 pb-12">

      <div>
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-3">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-700">Get started</h2>
          <span class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-700">~30 sec</span>
        </div>
        <div class="relative" data-copy-block>
          <pre class="code-block pr-20" tabindex="0" aria-label="Install commands"><code class="language-bash">mix archive.install hex francis
mix francis.new my_app</code></pre>
          <button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy hidden aria-label="Copy install commands">copy</button>
          <p class="sr-only" role="status" data-copy-status></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-3">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-700">Deploy</h2>
          <span class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-700">~2 min</span>
        </div>
        <div class="relative" data-copy-block>
          <pre class="code-block pr-20" tabindex="0" aria-label="Deploy commands"><code class="language-bash">mix francis.release
fly launch</code></pre>
          <button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy hidden aria-label="Copy deploy commands">copy</button>
          <p class="sr-only" role="status" data-copy-status></p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </section>

    <hr class="border-gray-200">

    <!-- The whole app: the fragments below, assembled -->
    <section class="pt-14 pb-12">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-3">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-700">The whole app</h2>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-700">lib/my_app.ex</span>
      </div>
      <pre class="code-block" tabindex="0" aria-label="A complete Francis app"><code class="language-elixir">defmodule MyApp do
  use Francis

  get "/", fn _ -> "Hello from Francis" end
  get "/users/:id", fn conn -> %{id: conn.params["id"]} end
  post "/echo", fn conn -> conn.body_params end

  ws "/ws", fn {:received, msg}, _socket -> {:reply, msg} end

  unmatched fn _ -> "not found" end
end</code></pre>
      <p class="primitive-note"><code class="font-mono">mix francis.new my_app</code> writes this file and the project around it. <code class="font-mono">iex -S mix francis.server</code> runs it.</p>
    </section>

    <hr class="border-gray-200">

    <!-- Features -->
    <section class="pt-14 pb-16">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-8">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-700">What you can build</h2>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-700">6 primitives</span>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-5">

        <div class="primitive-row">
          <p class="primitive-label">HTTP Actions</p>
          <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
            <pre class="primitive-code" tabindex="0" aria-label="HTTP actions example"><code class="language-elixir">get "/hello", fn _ -> %{hello: :world} end
get "/:name", fn %{params: params} -> params["name"] end
post "/", fn conn -> conn.body_params end</code></pre>
            <p class="primitive-note">Maps become JSON, strings are sent as-is &mdash; use <code class="font-mono">html/2</code> or <code class="font-mono">text/2</code> to set the type. URL params, body, and the raw conn always available.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="primitive-row">
          <p class="primitive-label">WebSockets</p>
          <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
            <pre class="primitive-code" tabindex="0" aria-label="WebSocket example"><code class="language-elixir">ws "/chat", fn
  :join, socket -> {:reply, "welcome"}
  {:received, msg}, _ -> {:reply, msg}
end</code></pre>
            <p class="primitive-note">Pattern match on join, close, incoming frames, and messages from other processes. Heartbeat and frame size limits included.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="primitive-row">
          <p class="primitive-label">Server-Sent Events</p>
          <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
            <pre class="primitive-code" tabindex="0" aria-label="Server-Sent Events example"><code class="language-elixir">sse "/events", fn
  :join, socket -> {:reply, %{event: "hello", data: socket.id}}
  {:received, update}, _ -> {:reply, update}
end

# from any process holding socket.transport
send(transport, %{event: "price", data: 42})</code></pre>
            <p class="primitive-note">Server to client only: push from any process via <code class="font-mono">send/2</code>. Named events, retry, and keepalive managed for you.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="primitive-row">
          <p class="primitive-label">Static Files</p>
          <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
            <pre class="primitive-code" tabindex="0" aria-label="Static files example"><code class="language-elixir">use Francis, static: [ from: "priv/static", at: "/" ]</code></pre>
            <p class="primitive-note">Serve from disk with gzip. Run <code class="font-mono">mix francis.digest</code> for content-hashed filenames and a cache manifest.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="primitive-row">
          <p class="primitive-label">Security</p>
          <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
            <pre class="primitive-code" tabindex="0" aria-label="Security example"><code class="language-elixir">plug Francis.Plug.SecureHeaders
plug Francis.Plug.CSP, directives: %{"script-src" =&gt; "'self'"}
safe_html conn, user_content  # auto-escapes &lt;&gt;&amp;&quot;'</code></pre>
            <p class="primitive-note">Secure headers and CSP with safe defaults &mdash; this page is served with both. Open redirects blocked in response helpers by design.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="primitive-row">
          <p class="primitive-label">Plug Ecosystem</p>
          <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
            <pre class="primitive-code" tabindex="0" aria-label="Plug ecosystem example"><code class="language-elixir">plug Plug.BasicAuth, username: "user", password: "pass"
plug Plug.Logger
plug MyApp.RateLimiter</code></pre>
            <p class="primitive-note">Any standard Plug middleware works. No lock-in, no adapters needed.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="border-gray-200">

    <!-- Honest disclaimer: practice what you preach -->
    <section class="py-12">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-700 mb-4">Honest about scope</h2>
      <p class="font-display text-base text-gray-700 leading-relaxed max-w-prose">
        Francis is a thin DSL on top of Plug and Bandit. If you need ORMs, generators, live views, or a full asset pipeline,
        reach for <a href="https://www.phoenixframework.org" class="text-link">Phoenix</a>.
        If you want to ship a small HTTP service in an afternoon, you are in the right place.
      </p>
    </section>

  </main>

  <footer class="border-t border-gray-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-10 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
        <span class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Francis</span>
        <span class="font-display text-sm text-gray-700">&middot; MIT licensed</span>
      </div>
      <nav class="flex gap-6 font-mono text-sm" aria-label="Project links">
        <a href="https://hexdocs.pm/francis/readme.html" class="inline-flex items-center min-h-11 text-gray-700 hover:text-gray-900 transition-colors">hexdocs</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/francis-build/francis" class="inline-flex items-center min-h-11 text-gray-700 hover:text-gray-900 transition-colors">github</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/francis-build/francis_site" class="inline-flex items-center min-h-11 text-gray-700 hover:text-gray-900 transition-colors">source</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </footer>

</body>
</html>
